export anchor IlluminatedManuscriptStyle:
    number: 144
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Illuminated manuscript
    idea: The dashboard is a page of a medieval book of hours, with vellum, ruled text blocks, a gilded drop capital for the greeting, red rubrics for headings and a vine growing down the margin.
    base: light
    palette:
        outerParchment: #e8d9b5, the page around the folio
        vellum: #f8f0dc, the folio, panels and fields
        ironGallInk: #2b1d10, body text and the chart baseline
        sepia: #5b4630, dates, notes, labels and italic asides
        rubric: #a3271c, rubric headings, pilcrows, overdue, Behind, this week bars and the primary button
        lapis: #22408a, the drop capital ground, last week bars, project links and focus
        goldLeaf: #b98a2e, frames, progress fills and the focus halo, never text
        goldInk: #6f4f12, At risk and the small roman numerals
        verdigris: #2e5e3b, the vine, the avatar and On track
        ruling: #d9b9a6, ruled lines and double margins
    type:
        Two old style serifs. Display uses Goudy Old Style, Garamond, EB
        Garamond, Palatino Linotype, Georgia, serif. Text uses Palatino
        Linotype, Book Antiqua, Palatino, URW Palladio L, Georgia, serif
        with old style numerals throughout. The drop capital is 76px bold
        white in a 104px box, the greeting 44px, summary figures 52px,
        rubrics 15px caps tracked 0.2em in red, entry titles 20px
        semibold, body 17px at 1.55, notes 14 to 15px italic, labels in
        small caps.
    layout:
        One folio up to 1260px on a darker parchment page. A 200px left
        margin holds the brand with a blue boxed initial B, an italic
        incipit, a Contents rubric and the nav as ruled lines each led by
        a red pilcrow, with a fleuron on the current page. A green vine
        with red and gold berries climbs the margin's right edge below the
        nav. The text block starts with a ruled header line holding an
        underlined italic search, a red New project button with a gold
        inner line, a round bell and a ringed avatar with the name in
        italic, closed by a red double rule. The greeting opens with a
        gilded lapis drop capital G beside the rest of the words, the date
        in italic and a red Take heed line naming the 4 overdue tasks. The
        four totals sit in one ruled row split by double rules, each with
        a small caps label, a large figure and a roman numeral beneath.
        Below, a wide Register of works lists the six projects as ruled
        entries with a large coloured initial alternating red and blue,
        the title and italic category, a gold striped progress rule,
        percent, tasks, due date and the status at the right. A narrower
        column holds the chart framed as a gilded miniature and a Chronicle
        of activity led by pilcrows. A colophon closes the page. Below
        900px the margin becomes a top strip with the nav in a row, the
        vine is hidden and columns stack.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 32 to 48px text margins, 40px between columns, 14px inside each register entry.
    density: Medium. A full text block per column, read slowly like a page.
    corners: Square, except a worn rounded top right corner on the folio and round arched tops on chart bars and swatches.
    borders: Red double rules under the header, a double ruling between margin and text, hairline ruling between entries and a gold frame with lapis and vellum rings around the miniature.
    shadows: None. Frames are layered rings of gold, vellum and lapis.
    icons:
        Thin line icons at text size, pilcrows and fleurons as markers.
        Status uses a green quatrefoil for On track, a gold brown triangle
        with a mark for At risk and a red crossed square for Behind, each
        beside the small caps word.
    focus: A 2px lapis outline offset 2 to 3px inside a 5 to 7px translucent gold halo. A focused field gets a lapis underline and a gold glow.
    tone: Gently archaic but clear, such as Good morrow, Mara, Take heed and The register of works.
